  "strategy": "### 1. Approach and rationale\nThe problem requires finding a step function \\( h: [0, 2] \\to [0, 1] \\) that minimizes the maximum overlap integral \\( C_5 \\), defined as:\n\\[ C_5 = \\max_k \\int_0^{2} h(x)(1 - h(x+k)) \\, dx \\]\nWe combine convex optimization with local search to escape local minima and improve the bound.\n\n### 2. Mathematical specification\nDefine \\( h \\) as a discretized function with \\( n_{\\text{points}} \\) samples. The objective is:\n\\[ C_5 = \\max_{k \\in [1, n_{\\text{points}} - 1]} \\left( \\sum_{i=0}^{n_{\\text{points}} - k - 1} h[i](1 - h[i + k]) \\cdot \\Delta x \\right) \\]\nsubject to:\n\\[ 0 \\leq h[i] \\leq 1 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\sum h[i] = \\frac{n_{\\text{points}}}{2} \\]\n\nWe use a convex relaxation by approximating \\( h \\) as a linear combination of basis functions in Fourier space, leveraging the convolution theorem to simplify overlap computation.\n\n### 3. Implementation procedure\n1. **Initialization**:\n   - Import initial_h_values as the starting point.\n   - Compute \\( \\Delta x = \\frac{2}{n_{\\text{points}}} \\).\n   - Ensure sum\u7ea6\u675f via scaling and clipping.\n\n2. **Convex Relaxation**:\n   - Formulate a convex optimization problem to minimize the maximum overlap.\n   - Use CVXPY with an interior-point solver to find an initial candidate.\n\n3. **Local Search Refinement**:\n   - Perturb small subsets of \\( h \\) iteratively.\n   - Use a gradient descent approach on the convex approximation.\n   - Ensure feasibility (sum and bounds) after each perturbation.\n\n4. **Constraint Handling**:\n   - After each update, redistribute values to satisfy \\( \\sum h[i] = \\frac{n_{\\text{points}}}{2} \\) without violating bounds.\n\n5. **Evaluation**:\n   - Compute \\( C_5 \\) using cross-correlation.\n   - Track the best solution and terminate if no improvement for 2 minutes.\n\n### 4. Search choices and variations\n- **Initialization**: Start with initial_h_values for basin hopping.\n- **Perturbation Size**: Begin with 10 indices, increase if stuck.\n- **Step Size**: Initial 0.01, adaptive based on progress.\n- **Termination**: Stop on local optimum or budget exhaustion.\n\n### 5. Compute budget and robustness\n- **Convex Optimization**: 10-20% of budget for initial solution.\n- **Local Search**: Primary solver with progress checks.\n- **Fallback**: Use the best feasible solution found, ensuring \\( C_5 \\leq 0.380876 \\).\n\n### 6. Validation and return\n- Ensure \\( h \\) satisfies constraints: \\( 0 \\leq h[i] \\leq 1 \\) and \\( \\sum h[i] = \\frac{n_{\\text{points}}}{2} \\).\n- Confirm \\( C_5 \\) via cross-correlation evaluation.",
